## Review expectations

- The `main` rulesets define the gate: `main-ci-required` (required status checks on
  an up-to-date branch) and `main-review-required` (one approving review, squash-only
  merges). Two approvals are not required.
- Reviewers look for scope discipline (one logical change), tests that can fail,
  verbatim error reporting, and secrets staying outside config and argv. See
  [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for the contributor side.
- A maintainer who is also the pull request author should not self-approve a change
  that touches a required-status-check workflow, the license, or `GOVERNANCE.md`.
- Maintainers are expected to follow the [Code of Conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) and to
  enforce it.

## Becoming a maintainer

- NomaDamas members may be granted maintainer rights by NomaDamas.
- External contributors may be approved as maintainers by NomaDamas after sustained,
  high-quality contributions — typically nominated by an existing maintainer with
  sign-off from the project lead.
- Maintainers who are inactive for an extended period may be moved to emeritus status
  by NomaDamas, and reinstated on return.

